# Gen-state bodies are a second full copy of all generated output — not worth
# committing. The MANIFEST is: `.hashes.json` is the only thing that lets
# `meta gen` tell "this file is exactly what I wrote" from "somebody edited
# this" on a machine that did not generate it (CLAUDE.md, Storage format).
#
# The glob matters. Git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a
# negation under `.gen-state/` can never apply — it has to be `.gen-state/*`.
.gen-state/*
!.gen-state/.hashes.json
